@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Uma Musume (JP) support
+
+Opens Uma Musume: Pretty Derby (JP, DMM/Steam) asset bundles so they load and export like any other Unity game.
+
+## How it works
+
+- `meta` (the game's asset database) is read with SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers (ChaCha20). It maps each
+  hash-named file in `dat/` to its asset name, dependencies and a per-file key.
+- Bundles are XOR-encrypted from offset 256 with a keystream built from the AB key and the per-file key
+  (`UmaCrypto`). Files with key 0 are loaded as-is.
+- The game folder is the one holding both `meta` and `dat`. It is found by walking up from a loaded file.
+
+## Setup
+
+1. Put `sqlite3mc_x64.dll` (Windows x64 build of SQLite3 Multiple Ciphers) in `AnimeStudio.Libraries/`
+   before building, or next to `AnimeStudio.GUI.exe` afterwards.
+2. Keys live in `UmaKeys.json` next to the executable (created with defaults on first use). Edit it if the
+   game changes keys; no rebuild needed.
+
+## Use
+
+1. Game selector: **Uma Musume (JP)**.
+2. **File > Load Uma Musume asset...**, pick the data folder (default
+   `%USERPROFILE%\AppData\LocalLow\Cygames\umamusume`), then enter one or more asset name prefixes separated
+   by `;`, e.g. `3d/chara/body/bdy1001_00; 3d/chara/head/chr1001_00`. Matches and all their dependencies
+   are loaded together.
+3. Export as usual (FBX via Animator, Texture2D, Material, AnimationClip).
+
+Loading hash-named files from `dat/` directly with Load file / Load folder also decrypts them.
+
+## Credits
+
+Encryption scheme and keys as implemented by UmaViewer (https://github.com/katboi01/UmaViewer).
